WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:05.205
The International Space Station (ISS) is a space station in low Earth orbit (LEO).

00:05.694 --> 00:19.070
It is the product of the International Space Station program and is operated by five partner space agencies: NASA, Roscosmos (Russia), ESA (Europe), JAXA (Japan), and CSA (Canada).

00:19.638 --> 00:28.433
It is the first space station built, maintained and crewed through international cooperation and the largest human spacecraft ever constructed.

00:29.079 --> 00:37.263
It is an orbital research station, where scientific experiments in microgravity are conducted and the space environment is studied.
